#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:1
msgid "ADR-0008: Sharing the GPU memory"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P2.2 (found while validating P4 and P6 on a GPU)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:9
#, python-format
msgid ""
"JAX reserves 75 % of the GPU memory when it creates its GPU client "
"(`XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE`, JAX documentation \"GPU memory "
"allocation\"). The memory reserved this way is only available to XLA: "
"cuFFT and cuBLAS workspaces, CuPy arrays and other processes must fit in "
"the rest. On a 6 GB GeForce GTX 1060 that also drives the Windows display"
" (about 2 GB used), the test suite run under WSL with the JAX CUDA "
"backend had 63 `CUDA_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY` failures; with preallocation "
"disabled, all tests passed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:15
msgid ""
"LUMOS users run on desktop and laptop GPUs shared with the display, and "
"LUMOS may use JAX and CuPy in the same process (REQ-HPC-1)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:18
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:20
msgid ""
"Before LUMOS loads the JAX backend or lists the JAX devices, it sets "
"`XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false` if the variable is not set "
"(`lumos.backend._core.prepare_jax`). JAX then allocates memory on demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:22
msgid ""
"A value set by the user (environment or `os.environ` before the first use"
" of a JAX device) is kept, so dedicated compute nodes can still "
"preallocate for speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:25
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:27
msgid ""
"**Keep the JAX default**: fastest allocation on dedicated GPUs, but out-"
"of-memory errors on shared ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:28
msgid ""
"**`XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_MEM_FRACTION`**: a fixed fraction is either too "
"large for small shared GPUs or too small for large computations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:30
msgid ""
"**Setting the variable when `lumos` is imported**: would also change the "
"behaviour of JAX code that does not use LUMOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:33
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:35
msgid ""
"JAX allocations are slightly slower (on demand) and memory may fragment "
"on long runs; users can set `XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=true` for "
"benchmarks on dedicated GPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0008-gpu-memory-sharing.md:37
msgid ""
"If the JAX GPU client already exists when LUMOS loads JAX (the user used "
"JAX first), the setting has no effect; this is documented."
msgstr ""
